# [Number of Sub-arrays With Odd Sum](https://leetcode.com/problems/number-of-sub-arrays-with-odd-sum/)

## Approach: Prefix Sum + Parity Counting

- Calculate the prefix sum array to store the cumulative sum up to each index.
- Maintain two counters:
  - `even`: Number of even prefix sums (initialized to 1 for the empty prefix).
  - `odd`: Number of odd prefix sums.
- A subarray has an odd sum when its two corresponding prefix sums have different parity.
- Traverse the prefix array:
  - If the current prefix sum is even, add `odd` to the answer and increment `even`.
  - If the current prefix sum is odd, add `even` to the answer and increment `odd`.
- Apply modulo \(10^9 + 7\) to avoid overflow.

## Code

```cpp
class Solution {
public:
    const int MOD = 1e9 + 7;

    int numOfSubarrays(vector<int>& arr) {
        int n = arr.size();
        vector<int> prefix;
        int sum = 0;

        for(int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
            sum += arr[i];
            prefix.push_back(sum);
        }

        int ans = 0, even = 1, odd = 0;

        for(int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
            if(prefix[i] % 2 == 0) {
                ans = (ans + odd) % MOD;
                even++;
            }
            else {
                ans = (ans + even) % MOD;
                odd++;
            }
        }

        return ans;
    }
};
```

## Complexity Analysis

- **Time Complexity:** \(O(n)\) — Two traversals of the array.
- **Space Complexity:** \(O(n)\) — Prefix sum array.
